*Apart from the three great empires and the true deities and Kings of Angels behind them, the Fourth Epoch also had the influence of the [[Demoness Sect]] and the [[Moses Ascetic Order]]. There was also the [[Abyss]]’ infiltration and secretly developed [[Church of the God of Steam and Machinery|Artisans]], as well as the [[Southern Continent]]’s Balam.
|-
|
|
|
*In addition, there were many crucial factors at stake. With the fading will of the [[Original Creator]]:
**The [[Original Creator#Astral Barrier|Barrier]] was weakening. Along with the death of the [[Ancient Sun God]], the invasion of reality by the Outer Deities clearly deepened.<ref name="C1348">{{Cite Book|1|1348}}</ref>
**The seal on the [[Western Continent]] by the [[Celestial Worthy of Heaven and Earth for Blessings]] was gradually weakening. The [[Sefirot]] instinctively (or consciously) used "Their" symbolism to corrode "Their" respective [[Uniqueness]] and High-Sequence Beyonder characteristics in an attempt to influence the outside world. In the Fourth Epoch, traces of more Sefirot began to appear on the Northern and Southern Continents and the islands over the Five Seas.<ref name="C1369" />
***The [[City of Calamity]] secretly seeped out energy from sealed [[Western Continent]], affecting the cities behind the door of [[Bansy Harbor|Binsy Town]].<ref>{{Cite Book|1|1339}}</ref><ref name="C1348" /><ref name="C1369" />
***The [[Nation of Disorder]] corrupted the Justiciar Uniqueness and turned it into the [[Trunsoest Brass Book]].<ref name="C1288" />
|-
|
|
|
*At the end of the Fourth Epoch, cracks appeared on the [[Original Creator#Astral Barrier|Barrier]]. The Seven Orthodox Gods had to move "Their" divine kingdoms to the [[Astral World]] to fill in the gap.<ref name="C1271">{{Cite Book|1|1271}}</ref>
